    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d194-a1">

                <pb facs="0474" n="378" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg378"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    107.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1879-04-29"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 29,
                    1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned has the honor, referring to the esteemed note of the chargé
                    d’affaires of the United States of America, Mr. H. Sidney Everett, of the 23d
                    instant, to transmit herewith a memorial concerning the principles which govern
                    in the matter of the employment in the military service of this country of
                    Prussian or German subjects who are in the private service of the foreign
                    missions here.</p>
                <p>While the undersigned at the same time takes the liberty to remark that he has in
                    the appropriate quarter made known the wish of Mr. H. Sidney Everett as to the
                    shortening of the military service of the servant Wilhelm Knoth, and that he
                    purposes making a further communication as soon as the shortly-to-be-expected
                    decision shall have been reached, he avails himself also of this occasion to
                    renew the expression of his distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">von</hi> BÜLOW.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Sidney Everett</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargè d’Affaires of the United States of
                            America.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
